00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.170
camera.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.330
Hi, mom.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.460
In

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:26.050
addition, all five operating
modes of the system were

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:31.190
evaluated, ranging from manual
operation by the astronauts to a

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.680
completely computer
-controlled operation.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.850
The three and a half hours of
tests done on the arm proved

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.200
highly successful.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:44.300
A real tribute to the designer,
the National Research Council of

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:48.180
Canada, and the builder,
SPAR Aerospace Limited.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.370
Canada absorbed all expenses
related to research and

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.500
development of
this first system.

00:16:57.270 --> 00:16:59.960
The first package of scientific
instruments to be flown on

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.700
shuttle from NASA's Office
of Space and Terrestrial

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:06.160
Applications was
designated OSTO -1.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:10.480
Although all the visual results
are not yet available from the

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:14.010
shuttle data takes, each
experiment is already flown on

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:15.370
aircraft or satellites.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:16.720
The

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:23.070
Shuttle Imaging Radar instrument
used side -looking radar to

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.800
create map -like images of the
Earth's surface, showing relief.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.850
When supplemented with
previously recorded Landsat

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.290
satellite data, which could
identify rocks and vegetation

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:38.640
types,

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:42.440
the composite revealed
geological structures of a type

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.620
which could possibly contain
valuable mineral deposits, such

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:47.030
as oil. With

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:52.290
the OSTA experiments mounted in
the payload bay of Space Shuttle

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:57.810
Columbia at an altitude of
160 miles, worldwide data was

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:01.920
obtained, proving that sensors
previously used on costly

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:06.290
individual satellites could now
be flown in groups on shuttle,

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.460
along with low -cost commercial
grade sensors that could only be

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.530
flown on aircraft before.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:16.410
This will greatly reduce the
cost of such experimentation in

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:19.210
the future, putting it
within reach of low -budget

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.560
researchers.

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:26.420
The ability to map Earth from
space also demonstrated the

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:29.780
potential for these instruments
to map other planets, yet

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:34.150
unexplored, even through dense
cloud cover, as the Shuttle

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:36.960
Imaging Radar experiment
was able to do.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:43.560
At the end of the second day,
Mission Control had a special

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:44.910
visitor.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:59.000
Let me just say, I'm sure you
know how proud everyone down

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:03.740
here is, and now this whole
nation, I'm sure the world, but

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:10.010
certainly America, has got
its eyes and its heart on you.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.360
We've

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.290
got the opportunity
to take part in this.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:23.030
We appreciate your taking the
trouble to show all the people

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.630
working on the space shuttle how
much you care and it makes us

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.980
mighty proud.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:33.720
I care and again, God bless you
both and all of us here, and are

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.670
watching with great pride.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:37.860
Thank you very much, sir.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.070
Thank you very much. Thank you

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.230
with all the priority
one objectives completed.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:52.920
The crew was ready to come home
Entry and landing would be their

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.270
last test

