00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:03.080
It did answer some
formidable questions.

00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:09.100
The orbiter is truly a reusable
spacecraft that can be launched

00:27:09.150 --> 00:27:10.930
again and again.

00:27:15.170 --> 00:27:18.480
Instruments in the payload bay
can map Earth's resources on a

00:27:18.530 --> 00:27:20.210
global scale and

00:27:23.860 --> 00:27:27.670
the remote manipulator system
has met this flight's test

00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:29.020
objectives.

00:27:30.200 --> 00:27:33.410
The completion of this flight
marks the halfway point in the

00:27:33.460 --> 00:27:35.120
Shuttle Flight Test Program.

00:27:36.220 --> 00:27:39.170
Columbia's third flight, a
mission of up to seven days

00:27:39.220 --> 00:27:42.820
duration, is scheduled
for the spring of 1982.

00:27:44.730 --> 00:27:48.520
The problems encountered so
far are not unexpected during

00:27:48.570 --> 00:27:50.250
developmental flight testing.

00:27:50.830 --> 00:27:55.120
Indeed, it is only through such
testing that confidence in the

00:27:55.170 --> 00:27:59.300
vehicle, its systems, and its
flying characteristics can be

00:27:59.350 --> 00:28:00.650
built.

00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:06.120
The Columbia is a totally new
concept in manned spaceflight.

00:28:06.940 --> 00:28:11.650
It needs very conservative, very
comprehensive testing before it

00:28:11.700 --> 00:28:13.320
can become operational.

00:28:14.330 --> 00:28:19.860
Making access to space something
it's never been before.

